            {
                "entry_id": "9629db84-36a5-391f-97ef-1894ef7acf21",
                "word": "kern",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8408c0e1-7f30-4570-935b-bf0f7a01baa3",
                        "entry_id": "9629db84-36a5-391f-97ef-1894ef7acf21",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "kerns"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18e3de3d-f519-338b-b079-eab181c1eb3e",
                        "entry_id": "9629db84-36a5-391f-97ef-1894ef7acf21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A light-armed foot soldier of the ancient militia of Ireland and Scotland; in archaic contexts often used as a term of contempt."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5191adce-f0c4-4732-840d-f1dda2931b4e",
                                "sense_id": "18e3de3d-f519-338b-b079-eab181c1eb3e",
                                "text": "O then belike she was old and gentle; and you rode like a kern of Ireland, your French hose off and in your strait strossers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bf02d79-a2a3-4977-91e4-5c9cf7666ec8",
                                "sense_id": "18e3de3d-f519-338b-b079-eab181c1eb3e",
                                "text": "‘O haste thee, and from Allan learn / If thou mayst trust yon wily kern.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2348f6d5-3355-402c-aef4-4d739e316cba",
                                "sense_id": "18e3de3d-f519-338b-b079-eab181c1eb3e",
                                "text": "There he entertained Shan O'Neil, a famous, turbulent chief from Ireland, who late in this year visited Elizabeth's Court, where his train of kerns and gallowglasses, clothed in linen kilts dyed with saffron, made a great impression."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d1f0a1c-00ca-489b-ae7f-6e16abd822f8",
                                "sense_id": "18e3de3d-f519-338b-b079-eab181c1eb3e",
                                "text": "In the pay-roll of Sir Ralph D'Ufford's expeditions in 1344, a mounted archer received 4d. a day, a foot archer 2d. and a kern, or simple foot-soldier 1d.13s \""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0b11f9f-4172-3d95-87d4-4527a7c13238",
                        "entry_id": "9629db84-36a5-391f-97ef-1894ef7acf21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A boor; a low person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ireland",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a552953-62d1-49a1-aa32-fbc0f5b7fa29",
                                "sense_id": "b0b11f9f-4172-3d95-87d4-4527a7c13238",
                                "text": "Yet it was held that the testimony of the common beadle of the parish, an officer of police, a vulgar, stupid kern, who stood before your own eyes, a very dolt to look on, in all the stark-staring hebetude of just wit enough to be spiteful—was to be credited as to the sense and meaning of an oration, his understanding was to be respected, and his representation trusted, where the Lord Chief Justice of England was in error."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ef1dd9b-72ec-4981-977b-c651890e97fa",
                                "sense_id": "b0b11f9f-4172-3d95-87d4-4527a7c13238",
                                "text": "To think that such a lowly kern Should dare to dream to be allied By wedlock to a royal bairn!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f38c4b5b-644b-445f-adad-700cd111d772",
                                "sense_id": "b0b11f9f-4172-3d95-87d4-4527a7c13238",
                                "text": "The kern was much puzzled, for never before had he known food bought or sold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e7ccde3-977a-4e0b-ba44-97e33255929f",
                                "sense_id": "b0b11f9f-4172-3d95-87d4-4527a7c13238",
                                "text": "The garrison were certain the Irish had no suitable equipment, that its manufacture was beyond the ignorant kern, and that it could not be bought for lack of funds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "807ba2af-8a8f-4db9-841a-5870f14b8ac0",
                                "sense_id": "b0b11f9f-4172-3d95-87d4-4527a7c13238",
                                "text": "Watch his impudent boldness with great men – you would not think that Essex was the premier Earl and that McGunn was the lowly kern from the boglands of Ireland."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "94ebcfc2-0a77-34b7-ac55-fe9499c00c22",
                        "entry_id": "9629db84-36a5-391f-97ef-1894ef7acf21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An idler; a vagabond."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "258aa018-2b2b-4bb7-98f3-a9541a7b8a87",
                                "sense_id": "94ebcfc2-0a77-34b7-ac55-fe9499c00c22",
                                "text": "The villain kernes Who keep me fettered here."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
